 "text": "Hey there, how are you doing right now? Try to keep them in small bags that you can get a good seal on. Use ice packs if you overfill the cooler. ice cubes are cheaper to use than blocks, and they melt slower. A thick towel around the cooler also helps keep the cold in. Keep the cooler out of direct sun and open it only a few times. A dry ice block on top will keep it cold all weekend. He gets hungry, you have to show him the food. Yes, every time you fill it up. Pour it out into the sink while the cold water is still cold.",
